      "mergeID": "65b97370a94f6fa84744b8fc",
      "mergedPostDetails": "And I guess all the other red items here.\n\nLet's begin with, any UdonSharp program using a line such as `someString.Trim('a');` would compile in Unity 2019, but will fail to compile in 2022 since the implicit cast to array no longer happens after the System.String.Trim(Char) method was added.\n\nThere is a workaround in the meantime, which is `someString.Trim(new[]{'a'});`.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "System.String.Trim(Char) is not exposed",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "65748d2db5e3b818abc3eb1b",
